hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21065","Waki narrated to us, Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Sumayr, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyyah, Bashir of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man walking in two sandals among the graves, and he said: O wearer of the two Sibtiyyahs, take them off."
"21066","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from a man of Banu Sadus called Daysam, he said: we said to Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyyah, he said: and his name had not been Bashir, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Bashir: we have neighbors of Banu Tamim, no stray of ours goes out except they take it, and things of their wealth come to us, shall we take them? He said: no."
"21067","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, a shaykh of Banu Sadus called Daysam narrated to me, from Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyyah, and he had come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he named him Bashir, then he mentioned the hadith."
"21068","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Aswad ibn Shayban informed us, from Khalid ibn Sumayr, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyyah, Bashir of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), holding his hand, and he said to me: O son of al-Khasasiyyah, what have you come to blame Allah, blessed and exalted is He, for in the morning? You have come to walk with His Messenger. He said: I think he said: holding his hand. He said: I said: I have not come to blame Allah for anything, Allah, blessed and exalted is He, has given me all good. He said: then we came upon the graves of the polytheists, and he said: these have been preceded by much good, three times. Then we came upon the graves of the Muslims, and he said: these have attained much good, three times, saying it. He said: then he saw a man walking among the graves in his sandals, and he said: woe to you, O wearer of the two Sibtiyyahs, take off your Sibtiyyahs, two or three times. Then the man looked, and when he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he removed his sandals."
"21069","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Aswad narrated to us, Khalid ibn Sumayr narrated to us, Bashir ibn Nahik narrated to us, he said: Bashir of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, and his name in the pre-Islamic period was Zahm ibn Mabad, then he migrated to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he asked him and said: what is your name? He said: Zahm. He said: no, rather you are Bashir. So that was his name. He said: while I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O son of al-Khasasiyyah, what have you come to blame Allah, blessed and exalted is He, for in the morning? You have come to walk with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Shayban, and he is al-Aswad ibn Shayban, said: I think he said: holding his hand. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, by my father and mother, I do not blame Allah, mighty and majestic is He, for anything. Then he mentioned the hadith, and he said: O wearer of the two Sibtiyyahs, take off your Sibtiyyahs."
"21070","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, she said: we used to prevent our young unmarried women from going out. Then a woman came and stayed at the palace of Banu Khalaf, and she narrated that her sister had been under a man of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who had raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twelve raids. My sister said: I raided with him six raids. She said: we used to treat the wounded and attend to the sick. Then my sister asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: is there harm upon one of us who has no outer garment if she goes out? He said: let her companion dress her from her outer garment, and let her witness good and the supplication of the believers. She said: when Umm Atiyyah came, I asked her, or we asked her: did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say such and such? She said: and she never mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that she said: may my father be sacrificed for him. Then she said: yes, may my father be sacrificed for him. He said: let the young unmarried women, those of seclusion, go out, or she said: the young unmarried women and those of seclusion, and menstruating women, so they witness good and the supplication of the believers, and the menstruating women keep away from the prayer place. Then I said to Umm Atiyyah: the menstruating woman? She said: do they not witness Arafah and witness such and witness such?"
